This <University of Oxford> Part A options paper covers fourteen printed sections and nineteen questions. https://www.whatdotheyknow.com/request/maths_papers_2/response/1850333/attach/3/FOI%2020210708%201%20Data.zip?cookie_passthrough=1[Source release]{ref} The archive contains the complete editable eleven-page transcription. Bounded official-source searches found no advertised answers to this exact paper. All 30 source leaves and their unnumbered tasks are covered below. The source's mechanics potential is retained in the transcription, and its physical interpretation is qualified in the solution. The string-length and statistical-distribution assumptions are also made explicit where needed.

